lifeos-nix patch f-launcher-cwd — default to the current directory, not ~/.claude

PROBLEM
  The `lifeos` launcher (LIFEOS/TOOLS/lifeos.ts) chdir'd to the config root (~/.claude) before
  spawning Claude Code on EVERY launch, unless the user passed --local. So a session opened
  anywhere (a project, a dev dir) landed with cwd = ~/.claude — Claude sees the LifeOS config
  tree instead of the project the user is actually in. For a dev-first workflow that is the
  wrong default; the useful case (session in the config root for LifeOS-meta work) is the rare one.

FIX (invert the default)
  Default is now stay-in-current-directory. Opt in to the config root with --claude-dir / -c.
  --local is kept as a no-op alias for the now-default behavior (back-compat). Both the
  interactive launch (cmdLaunch) and the one-shot (cmdPrompt) honor this; the one-shot's
  unconditional chdir is removed. CLI flag, dispatch, KNOWN_FLAGS allowlist, help text, and
  docstring updated.

  GUARD RE-KEY (7.40.4 migration, 2026-08-27): 7.40.4 added a worktree-safety guard (public
  PR #1579) keyed on `options.local` — it refuses a main-checkout-with-worktrees launch that
  would run on the parked branch. That guard protects the STAY-IN-CWD behaviour, but keys on
  the --local FLAG. Our default-inversion divorces the two: stay-in-cwd becomes the flag-less
  default, so a guard reading `options.local` would go silent for the exact dangerous case it
  exists to catch. Re-keyed to `!options.claudeDir` so it fires whenever the session actually
  stays in cwd (the new default); a --claude-dir session cd's away and correctly skips it.

SCOPE / CO-EXISTENCE
  One file (lifeos.ts): docstring / cmdLaunch (sig + guard + chdir) / cmdPrompt / help /
  KNOWN_FLAGS / arg-parse / dispatch. Disjoint from f4-a (update-check fns only). Re-generated
  against the 7.40.4 tree (2026-08-27 migration).

VERIFICATION
  `lifeos` stays in cwd; `lifeos -c` runs in ~/.claude; `lifeos --local` still works (no-op);
  the worktree guard still fires on a default (flag-less) launch in a main checkout. Hunks via
  `git diff`, never hand-counted.

